### /tmp/guide-release/marqdo-3.0.0-beta.1-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/marqdo --help
Marqdo executes .mq.md documents: headings declare @exec/@knowledge modes, Strong/Emph/inline Code carry one statement each, and if/else/while/end/return/params decide control flow. `check` and `inspect` never execute project code; `run` and `call` execute through the capability host.

Usage: marqdo <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init     Initialise a new Marqdo project
  run      Run the entry function (`main` by default) of a document
  call     Call a named function with typed arguments
  check    Statically check a document without executing it
  inspect  Inspect AST, units, signatures, IR, references or platform support
  fmt      Conservative formatting: normalises line endings and trailing newlines
  plugin   Plugin artifact inspection (never loads plugin code)
  add      Add a dependency to marqdo.yaml
  remove   Remove a dependency from marqdo.yaml
  lock     Generate a deterministic marqdo.lock for the current project
  sync     Verify that path dependencies match the lockfile
  tool     Manage and dispatch generic external CLI tools
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
